        rdf:type                        "vstoi:Instrument" ;
        rdfs:comment                    "An obstetric simulator is a specialized training tool designed to replicate various aspects of childbirth and prenatal care, enabling healthcare professionals and students to practice and enhance their obstetric skills in a controlled, risk-free environment. These simulators range from basic anatomical models to advanced, computer-controlled manikins that mimic realistic physiological responses during labor and delivery." ;
