pmsr:OBJ_instrumentcollection_INS1739301317613705
        rdf:type                        "vstoi:Instrument" ;
        rdfs:comment                    "An Automated External Defibrillator (AED) is a portable medical device designed to treat individuals experiencing sudden cardiac arrestÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€ Ã¢â‚¬â„¢ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬Ãƒâ€¦Ã‚Â¡ÃƒÆ’Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã†â€™Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¢ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…Â¡Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¬ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¯Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â¿Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â½a condition where the heart unexpectedly stops beating. The AED analyzes the heart's rhythm and, if it detects an abnormality such as ventricular fibrillation or pulseless ventricular tachycardia, delivers an electric shock (defibrillation) to help restore a normal heartbeat. These devices are user-friendly, featuring audio and visual prompts to guide even untrained bystanders through the process, making them essential tools in emergency situations to improve survival rates." ;
        rdfs:label                      "Automated External Defibrilator" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf                 "ncit:C80461" ;
        hasco:hasDataAcquisition        "http://example.org/roundtrip/DA-DA-SOC-INSTRUMENT-PMSR.csv" ;
        hasco:hasDataAcquisition        <http://example.org/roundtrip/DA-DA-SOC-INSTRUMENT-PMSR.csv> ;
        hasco:hasDataFile               "http://example.org/roundtrip/DFL-DA-SOC-INSTRUMENT-PMSR.csv" ;
        hasco:hasTimestamp              "2026-06-03T19:41:26.495Z" ;
        hasco:hasTotalRecordedMessages  "0" ;
        hasco:hasWebDocument            "https://www.heart.org/-/media/files/health-topics/answers-by-heart/what-is-an-aed.pdf" ;
        hasco:hascoType                 "vstoi:Instrument" ;
        vstoi:hasInstrument             "pmsr:INST-INS1739301317613705" ;
        vstoi:hasLanguage               "pmsr:/en" ;
        vstoi:hasShortName              "pmsr:/AutomatedExternalDefibrilator" ;
        vstoi:hasStatus                 "UNPROCESSED" ;
        vstoi:hasVersion                "pmsr:/1" .

pmsr:OBJ_instrumentcollection_INS1739392275798255
        rdf:type                        "vstoi:Instrument" ;
        rdfs:comment                    "The Resusci Anne QCPR AED is an adult manikin designed for the Laerdal LINK system. The special LINK electrodes can be used for training with the Philips Heartstart FR2 and FR3 training devices. LINK technology gives you feedback on the correct placement of the electrodes. The model has been equipped with various feedback options that allow objective visualization of CPR performance. All feedback devices clearly indicate how the student can improve their CPR skills. The full-body version offers a realistic training scenario. Resusci Anne QCPR can be easily transported using the practical carrying case. The scope of delivery also includes a training mat on which the mannequin is placed and which serves as a support for the students' knees." ;
        rdfs:label                      "ResusciAnne DAE Simulator" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf                 "pmsr:/INS1739392182337835" ;
        hasco:hasDataAcquisition        "http://example.org/roundtrip/DA-DA-SOC-INSTRUMENT-PMSR.csv" ;
